-## Technical stack
+- The historical JPEG-Q55 study completed 30/30 visual-channel trials for one
+  document, one authority/codebook and one recipient identity across repeated
+  sessions. It is not the current strict PDF verdict, a multi-person experiment
+  or physical performance.
+- Five one-page marked PDFs preserved extracted text and averaged about 41.87 dB
+  rendered PSNR. They are not byte-identical PDFs, a human invisibility study or
+  proof that pre-existing PDF signatures survive.
+- The 30-codebook × 4-strategy study contains 120 code-level cases. These are not
+  120 carrier, PDF or physical trials.
 
-- **Cryptography:** ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204), AES-256-GCM,
-  HKDF-SHA3-256 and AES-CTR-derived codebook streams.
-- **Fingerprint:** original one-sided binary Tardos accusation score, 52,500 binary symbols,
-  keyed 6 x 6 rendering blocks, 72-bit HMAC layout tag with Hamming(7,4), and
-  fail-closed channel consensus; all 1,000 rows scored.
-- **Prototype:** Python, OpenSSL provider, PyMuPDF, NumPy, Pillow, OpenCV ORB and
-  RANSAC homography registration.
-- **Offline provenance:** quorum-signed recipient enrollment root, four
-  demonstrator replicas, 3-of-4 ML-DSA endorsement, hash-linked blocks, and a
-  separately signed ledger-head witness.
-- **Deployment:** signed controlled viewer, offline CA, TPM/HSM recipient keys,
-  and separately administered Hyperledger Fabric peers.
-- **No cloud dependency:** no hosted KMS, model/API, public blockchain,
-  cryptocurrency or internet connection.
+Evidence: `artifacts/nishan/end-to-end-jpeg-trials.json`,
+`artifacts/nishan/tardos-independent-codebook-study.json` and
+`artifacts/nishan/tardos-pdf-benchmark.json`.
 
-## Main risks and gates
+### Physical evidence remains experimental
 
-| Risk | Current truth | Gate before a broad claim |
-|---|---|---|
-| Editable-PDF carrier removal | Either carrier is removable; one leaves a lead and forces abstention, both leave no signal | Content-bound carrier plus controlled viewer; keep agreement policy |
-| JPEG/print/photo violates the marking assumption | JPEG and synthetic geometry are empirical; physical hardware remains unmeasured | Run the prepared 150/300-DPI print-scan and phone-camera protocol |
-| Carrier transplantation frames another session | One-channel policy was vulnerable | Editable PDFs now require agreement; transplant and transplant-then-strip both abstain |
-| Mathematical bound is repeated as a physical guarantee | Code theorem and carrier condition are separate in every evidence file | Predeclare attack and inspect unanimous-position errors; never transfer the bound silently |
-| Source needed for extraction | Detector is non-blind | Protected source archive, hash-bound chain of custody, then evaluate blind synchronization |
-| Recipient can capture plaintext before marking | Trusted endpoint assumed | Signed viewer, restricted export, device attestation and protected rendering |
-| Demo operator owns all keys | PQ mechanisms are real; custody is synthetic | Offline CA, employee binding, HSM/TPM keys and separate validator administrators |
-| All ledger replicas are rolled back together | The ledger accepts the valid prefix; the external witness detects it | Retain checkpoints and witness key outside ledger administration |
-| Dishonest distributor can frame a recipient | Authority controls both carrier secrets | Buyer-involved asymmetric fingerprinting and independent adjudication |
-| Concurrent row assignment | Current demo is sequential | Transactional allocation committed by quorum before rendering |
+- The shipped historical threshold recovered 0/4 real captures.
+- Both exploratory conditional profiles recovered the same one capture,
+  `akshay3.jpeg`, so the result is 1/4 per profile—not two captures.
+- The study uses one printed single-page public fixture and is visual code-row
+  research, not end-to-end signed physical attribution or a reliability rate.
 
-## Three-minute demonstration
+Evidence: `research/evidence/nishan-bias-physical-2026-09-10/scores.json`.
 
